# README Lifecycle Engineering — standalone Ec-compatible skill candidate

This package contains **one new candidate skill**, formatted like the supplied Ec skills:
`SKILL.md` with `name`/`description` frontmatter, progressive `references/` and an optional
SDD bridge. Its optional `agents/openai.yaml` follows the Ox UI metadata convention.

## Scope

Create, restructure and maintain repository and package READMEs through product growth.
The central principle is **one discoverable README entry point plus canonical task-oriented
documentation where needed**, not one giant mandatory file and not one file per feature.

## Installation (manual, after project authorization)

Copy `skills/readme-lifecycle-engineering/` (the complete folder) under the consumer's
real skills directory. If the consuming project uses SDD 1.3.0 and wants a bridge,
copy `sdd/chain/readme-lifecycle-engineering.md` and replace `UNCONFIGURED` with the
actual project-relative path to its `SKILL.md`.

The skill works independently of SDD and other skills. Installation, invocation, profile
adoption, changes to the Ec README and compliance acceptance are separate steps; this
artifact does **not** perform any of them.

## Source discipline

Method based on GitHub, Google, GitLab and Diátaxis guidance; university resources from
Harvard, Cornell, Johns Hopkins, Toronto, Singapore Management University and Monash;
and peer-reviewed studies described with scopes and limits in
`skills/readme-lifecycle-engineering/references/sources-and-decisions.md` and
`skills/readme-lifecycle-engineering/references/scientific-evidence-and-limits.md`.

## Relation to the prior catalog

The previous 66-entry recommendation is unchanged until this new skill is deliberately
adopted. This candidate would be **entry 67** if adopted without replacing another entry.
It **does overlap** general documentation at the margins; the selection boundary is explicit
in `references/routing-and-oracles.md` to avoid redundant activation.

## Applicable Ec norms

`EC-REGRAS-DE-DESIGN-E-PRODUTO.md` (primary), with
`EC-REGRAS-CRIACAO-DE-TELAS-E-IMAGENS.md` consulted for README screenshots and UI evidence.
No existing product configuration, skill or SDD record was changed. Any discrepancy between
current Ec norms and exploratory architecture (e.g., gRPC vs versioned HTTP) stays a
**proposal** until adopted by the authorized architecture process.
